# Why almost-full hospital wards keep patients waiting
subtitle: "Why a hospital ward that is nine-tenths full keeps patients waiting so much longer than one that is half full — and why the last few beds matter most."
tags: ["hospital waiting times","queueing theory","bed occupancy","health services","capacity planning"]
teaches: ["concepts/queueing-utilisation","concepts/spare-capacity"]
thumb: "band \"95 % full. What could go wrong?\" note \"5 % spare = 2× wait\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a clear, warm explainer, unhurried","b":"gemini:Puck | a relaxed, good-humoured co-host with a dry, understated wit; never exaggerated"}

## Why almost-full hospital wards keep patients waiting
use: equation_plot
with:
    equation: W = h*x/(100 - x)
    params:
      h: {value: 1, fixed: true}
      u: {value: 50, min: 40, max: 97, step: 1, label: beds full}
    editable:
      - u
    x_range:
      - 40
      - 100
    y_range:
      - 0
      - 40
    x_label: '% full'
    y_label: Wait for a bed (h)
    marks:
      - {kind: point, at: u, id: lp}
sources:
    - id: bagust
      title: 'Dynamics of bed use in accommodating emergency admissions: stochastic simulation model'
      authors: Bagust A, Place M, Posnett JW
      year: 1999
      finding: Risks appear once average bed occupancy exceeds about 85 %; at 90 % or more, regular bed shortages and periodic bed crises.
      doi: 10.1136/bmj.319.7203.155

    path wall dashed #8f887c points [[100,0],[100,40]] data true hidden true
    label lwall "Full" above #8f887c attach_to wall font_size 30 hidden true
    path naive dashed #8f887c points [[40,0.8],[100,2]] data true hidden true
    label lnaive "in step?" above #8f887c attach_to naive font_size 30 hidden true
    dot p50 #3d3833 at.data [50,1] style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label p50_label "1 h" above-left attach_to p50 font_size 30 hidden true
    dot p80 #3d3833 at.data [80,4] style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label p80_label "4 h" above-left attach_to p80 font_size 30 hidden true
    dot p90 #3d3833 at.data [90,9] style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label p90_label "9 h" above-left attach_to p90 font_size 30 hidden true
    dot p95 #3d3833 at.data [95,19] style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label p95_label "19 h" above-left attach_to p95 font_size 30 hidden true
    scale guess x 200 y 520 width 420 label "Wait at 95 % full" unit hours min 0 max 40 value 19 hidden true
    polygon band10 thin #2f6b8f points [[90,0],[100,0],[100,40],[90,40]] data true style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.18 hidden true
    label lb10 "10 % spare" left #2f6b8f attach_to band10 font_size 30 hidden true
    polygon band5 thin #2f6b8f points [[95,0],[100,0],[100,40],[95,40]] data true style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.3 hidden true
    label lb5 "5 % spare" left #2f6b8f attach_to band5 font_size 30 hidden true
    math fx tex "\\text{wait} \\propto \\frac{\\text{busy}}{\\text{spare}}" colors {"\\text{spare}":"#2f6b8f"} x 330 y 560 hidden true
    scratch ev work ["Bad night: +5 patients","10 spare a day → ½ day","1 spare a day → 5 days"] x 360 y 390 hidden true
    polygon cut_lo thin #8a5fa8 points [[55,0],[60,0],[60,40],[55,40]] data true style.fill #8a5fa8 style.opacity 0.3 hidden true
    label lcut_lo "55–60" above #8a5fa8 attach_to cut_lo font_size 30 hidden true
    polygon cut_hi thin #8a5fa8 points [[90,0],[95,0],[95,40],[90,40]] data true style.fill #8a5fa8 style.opacity 0.3 hidden true
    label lcut_hi "90–95" above #8a5fa8 attach_to cut_hi font_size 30 hidden true
    group opt_lo members ["cut_lo","lcut_lo"] hidden true
    group opt_hi members ["cut_hi","lcut_hi"] hidden true
    path many smooth dashed #8f887c points [[40,0],[45,0],[50,0],[55,0],[60,0.01],[65,0.02],[70,0.05],[75,0.13],[80,0.34],[85,0.95],[90,2.82],[95,10.81],[96,15.32],[97,23.13],[97.5,29.52],[98,39.24]] data true hidden true
    label lmany "many beds" below-right #8f887c attach_to many font_size 30 hidden true
    path m85 dashed #8f887c cites ["bagust"] points [[85,0],[85,40]] data true hidden true
    label l85 "85 %" above #8f887c attach_to m85 cites ["bagust"] font_size 30 hidden true
    label lread "{eq.u} % → {eq.lp_y:0} h" left #b5482e attach_to lp font_size 30 hidden true

    card title "Why almost-full wards wait"

    hide equations

Why do waits for a hospital bed explode when a ward is almost, but not quite, (@draw wall lwall ends@) full?
    draw axes

B: Surely a (@draw naive lnaive@) ward at 95 % full is only a little worse than one at 90? (@point at.ref naive gesture underline@) The wait just grows in step.

That's the natural guess. Take the simplest queue, with (@draw p50 p50_label@) made-up numbers: say a patient waits an hour for a bed when the ward is half full.

Fill it (@draw p80 p80_label@) to 80 %, and the wait is four hours; at 90 %, (@draw p90 p90_label ends@) nine.

B: So what happens at 95 %, just five points fuller?
    draw guess

    ask "Click the line where you think the wait at 95 % full lands." on guess store g
        right: Close: you said {g}; it is {g.true}.
        wrong: You said {g}; it is {g.true}.

Five more points of fullness, and the wait has more than doubled.
    draw p95 p95_label

B: Doubled? Why would five points matter so much?
    erase naive lnaive

Because patients do not arrive evenly: some nights bring (@flow curve_0@) a rush, and only the beds still free can soak it up.
    draw curve_0

At 90 % full, a tenth of the capacity is spare; at 95 %, only a (@draw band5 lb5 ends@) twentieth.
    draw band10 lb10

The wait follows busy divided by spare, so halving (@highlight fx part \text{spare}@) the spare share about doubles the wait.
    draw fx

    erase band10 lb10 band5 lb5

B: What does that mean on a bad night, say five extra admissions?
    draw ev_box ev_line_1

A ward that can discharge twenty (@highlight p50@) a day but takes in ten has ten spare a day, and catches up within half a day.
    draw ev_line_2

At 95 % full it takes in nineteen (@highlight p95@) and has one spare a day: five days to catch up, and the next bad night comes first.
    draw ev_line_3

    erase ev

    draw opt_lo opt_hi parallel true

    ask "Where would freeing five points of room cut the wait most? Tap that band." choose ["opt_lo","opt_hi"] answer opt_hi store c stage own
        right: Yes: there it more than halves the wait, from nineteen hours to nine.
        wrong: Down at 55 to 60 it saves only about a quarter of an hour: the spare share barely changes.

    erase opt_lo opt_hi

B: But a real ward has dozens of beds. Doesn't that change things?
    highlight curve_0

It softens it: a ward (@draw many lmany@) with many beds stays flat for longer, but the wall at full (@highlight wall@) stays where it is.

Even so, above about 85 (@draw m85 l85@) % full the bad nights start leaving no bed free at all now (@point at.ref p90 gesture circle@) and then: that is where a well-known 1999 study found the risks begin.

    erase m85 l85 many lmany

    draw lp lread

Try it: drag the dot along the curve, and watch the wait climb the wall.
    animate params.u.value 96 duration 4

    explore

B: So it's not really how full the ward is.
    erase lp lread

No: it's how little room is left to absorb bad luck — and near full, that room vanishes fast.
    highlight curve_0

    quiz "If every patient arrived exactly on schedule, evenly spaced, and every stay lasted exactly as long, what would the wait be at 95 % full?"
        right: Hardly any: with no bad nights and no surprise stays, there is never a rush for the spare beds to absorb.
        wrong: Ask what the spare beds were absorbing in the first place.
        * About 19 hours, as before
        * Even longer
        + Hardly any wait

That is why some hospitals now spread planned operations evenly across the week: they cannot remove the bad nights, but they can stop adding their own.
    highlight curve_0

## Thumbnail
domain:
    x:
      - 0
      - 100
    'y':
      - 0
      - 25
    box:
      x: 120
      'y': 290
      w: 780
      h: 420
role: thumbnail

    axes ax x_label "Beds full" y_label Wait hidden true
    curve c #b5482e expr x/(100-x) x_from 0 x_to 96 style.stroke_width 7 hidden true
    path w dashed #8f887c points [[100,0],[100,25]] data true style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    icon bed size 150 set twemoji x 330 y 560 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    thumb b "95 % full. What could go wrong?" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    text a1 "90 % full" #2f6b8f x 270 y 560 font_size 64 hidden true
    text a2 "9 hours" #3d3833 x 720 y 560 font_size 64 hidden true
    text b1 "95 % full" #b5482e x 270 y 380 font_size 64 hidden true
    text b2 "?" #b5482e x 720 y 380 font_size 120 hidden true
    icon clock size 110 set twemoji x 500 y 470 icon_look picture of hourglass hidden true
    thumb b "5 points fuller…" kind band hidden true
    thumb s "GUESS" kind stamp x 160 y 660 angle 10 hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon bd0 size 95 set twemoji x 150 y 600 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd1 size 95 set twemoji x 325 y 600 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd2 size 95 set twemoji x 500 y 600 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd3 size 95 set twemoji x 675 y 600 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd4 size 95 set twemoji x 850 y 600 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd5 size 95 set twemoji x 150 y 470 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd6 size 95 set twemoji x 325 y 470 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd7 size 95 set twemoji x 500 y 470 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    icon bd8 size 95 set twemoji x 675 y 470 icon_look picture of bed hidden true
    text bd9 "1 free" #2f6b8f x 850 y 470 font_size 40 hidden true
    icon q size 110 set twemoji x 200 y 300 icon_look picture of person hidden true
    icon q2 size 110 set twemoji x 320 y 300 icon_look picture of person hidden true
    icon q3 size 110 set twemoji x 440 y 300 icon_look picture of person hidden true
    thumb b "The last free beds matter most" kind band hidden true
    thumb n "queue maths" kind note x 780 y 300 angle -6 hidden true
